{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:ad5633f046200c3b0e3991c4f632c736e37cd55dfafdaa90f1741d2f8686366c","grain":"paper-statement","id":"Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026#l:finite-entropy:regularization","title":"Finite expected regularization"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/e2ede620541a8010974acb1c.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Lemma","generation_id":"sha256:fda4c3462963b650c538e2177794811eb1c221b267efea4b091fd6e397533f81","id":"r:Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026:l:finite-entropy:regularization","kind":"statement-detail","manuscript_id":"p:Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026","name":"Finite expected regularization","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","printed_number":null,"printed_number_provenance":null,"printed_number_status":"unavailable","reading_page":"papers/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026.html#l:finite-entropy:regularization","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":5,"section_title":"Regularization from finite relative entropy","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:82421e1edf8ab47514c377593321c6cc33aabb363a4328b01780c50d566e8761","file":"preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/drafts/dyadic-entropy/finite-entropy.tex","line":47,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":null,"provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/drafts/dyadic-entropy/finite-entropy.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:82421e1edf8ab47514c377593321c6cc33aabb363a4328b01780c50d566e8761","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Localization-costs-and-information-growth-for-exact-Gaussian-observations-September-27-2026/build/sections/drafts/dyadic-entropy/finite-entropy.tex#L47"},"statement_kind":"lemma","text":"\\label{l:finite-entropy:regularization}\nSuppose \\(P\\ll\\mu_C\\) and \\(K_0=D(P\\Vert\\mu_C)<\\infty\\).\nFor all sufficiently large \\(n\\), a countable label determined by\n\\(W\\sim P\\) specifies a descendant \\(C'\\) and a conditional law\n\\(P'\\) regular on \\(C'\\).  The label is the whole terminating\nhistory in the construction below, including every complement\ndecision; \\(P'\\) is conditioned on this label and need not be\n\\(P(\\,\\cdot\\mid C')\\).\n\nLet \\(H\\) be the increase in cell depth and \\(A_*\\) the number of\nattempts.  Then\n\\[\n \\mathbb EH<\\infty,\\qquad\n \\mathbb EA_*\\le2(1+\\mathbb EH)<\\infty,\n\\]\nand, with \\(b=(1-\\alpha)(\\log2)/2\\),\n\\begin{equation}\\label{l:finite-entropy:budget}\n \\mathbb E D(P'\\Vert\\mu_{C'})+bn\\,\\mathbb EH\\le K_0+2/e.\n\\end{equation}\nThe hypothesis imposes no boundedness on \\(dP/d\\mu_C\\)."}
